# Secrets: the FTP login used by buildall.ps1 and buildweb.ps1
# (the committed example is ftp-config.example.ps1), and the server's own
# config.php - database password and the licence private key
# (the committed template is server/config.sample.php).
ftp-config.ps1
server/config.php
# The shop's secrets (SMTP login, payment API keys). The sample says to keep it
# outside the web root, but one dropped next to the PHP would otherwise be committed.
shop-config.php
# what the FTP upload last sent (scripts/ftp-changed.ps1)
.ftp-state.json

# Build output and published downloads: never committed. GitHub refuses a push holding
# any file over 100 MB (a 170 MB Linux download is what broke a release on 2026-11-12);
# the installers are published to the web site by FTP instead.
binaries-old/
*.exe
*.zip
website/dist/downloads/
